  "notes": "Written as an artist entry only, on the research's own instruction — Timbaland's existing model supplies her production lane, so what is encoded here is her vocal-rhythm design and arrangement signature, 1997–2005. Tempo is \"81–102 straight (backbeat 2&4)\" and the entry folds the 178 reading back to \"an 89 spine with double-time percussion\", so the mode is 89 and `halfTime` stays false. The three drum deltas follow her stated contribution — \"placement of *voice* on the grid — ad-libs, grunts, reversed syllables and 'pings and bips and bloops' used as percussion, filling the 16ths the kit leaves empty\" — which is a six-lane percussion bed at 4–8 hits a bar and −2 dB, the densest and most forward in the whole section, against a hat lane cut to 0.3 and a snare held dead flat on the grid (`offGridMs` 0) because \"the backbeat stays flat on 2&4 so the vocal can syncopate against it\". Harmony is \"near-static… one chord or a two-chord modal shuttle\", so single- and two-chord families with a long duration range. \"A 'singsong' flow that sits between rap and melody, chant-and-response phrases in 2-bar cells, and a sung hook of 3–5 pitches\" gives `structure` `call_response`, `twoBarCellRepeat`, a 3–5 pitch motif and a riff-dominant contour. The bass is \"one-note or two-note sub riffs, long gaps, no chordal bass\" — a real bass part rather than a `bass808` block, with a near-1.0 root follow and single-degree cells. ⚠ Confidence is medium: the research rates it high-medium and notes the vocal-rhythm description is \"sourced to critical analysis rather than to a technique interview\". ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are all velocity and density numbers and `swing.amount` 0.56. ⚠ **`chords.harmonicRhythm` re-weighted (2026-08-17, harmony variety floor).** The entry gives the one-chord and the two-chord bed equal billing — \"near-static harmony (one chord or a two-chord modal shuttle) ... chant-and-response phrases in 2-bar cells\" — and the engine's `vamp` value is *one* chord held for the whole clip (`generators::chords`: \"One chord for the whole pattern\"), so a `vamp` weight of 6-of-8 made the two-chord half of that sentence almost unreachable. `vamp` keeps the top weight; the two-chord reading is now reachable at both rates. ⚠ The split between those two rates is **INFERRED** — the entry names the device, not its rate.",
